Xynolog protocol work

Beginning 2026-08-27, Xynolog formalized and substantially expanded the
protocol into machine-readable, validated specifications: OpenAPI definitions
for the Gateway and Archivist HTTP APIs; a machine-readable definition of the
launcher Control API; JSON Schema definitions for shared wire types and
service configuration, health, and messages; normative protocol contracts;
registries; and behavioral and conformance cases. The August 26 snapshot
records an earlier protocol instance. The post-boundary protocol model is
general enough to represent it. The snapshot does not contain the formal
model, OCaml reader and validator, or code-generation system built afterward.
The reader validates the specifications, and the code-generation system
produces protocol artifacts for nine SDK languages. This repository specifies
protocol interfaces and behavior; service runtime implementations and image
details are maintained in their respective repositories. This post-boundary
work was authored by Adam Pingel.

Baseline snapshot

The repository's root commit, 033f0de, preserves protocol material from The
AI Alliance's Semiont monorepo through 2026-08-26. It records an earlier
protocol instance and the provenance of that material, which remains under
the Apache License, Version 2.0. See HISTORY-MAP.md. The Semiont attribution
identifies the snapshot's provenance; it does not describe authorship of the
structure built afterward.

Third-party notices remain with the files or dependencies to which they apply.
